{%- comment -%}
  Hero event badge (seal sticker). Renders the Theme Editor copy first so the
  seal is never empty and nothing jumps, then theme.js repaints it in place
  from PawScout's /public/event feed (ONE fetch per page view, shared with the
  welcome modal and the announcement bar; feed cached 10 minutes server-side,
  120 seconds in the browser):
    - a running event: its name, then "<pct>% off with code <code>" (plus
      "until <end>" when it fits the seal), linking to all products;
    - nothing running but a planned event: "Next: <name>" and its dates.
      Name and dates only: codes and percentages are never announced ahead;
    - nothing running and nothing planned: the seal hides. A seasonal stamp
      that cannot be checked against the calendar is exactly the stale
      "summer" badge the owner asked to retire;
    - feed unreachable or malformed: the copy below stays, untouched.
  Every word a visitor reads in the two feed states comes from the feed. The
  emoji for those states live here rather than in JS so a copy tweak never
  needs a script change. Sizes for feed copy are scoped below instead of in
  theme.css: event names and date ranges run longer than the two-word stamp
  the seal was drawn for.
{%- endcomment -%}
<a
  class="hero-event-badge"
  data-event-badge
  data-event-badge-href="{{ routes.all_products_collection_url }}"
  data-event-emoji-active="🎉"
  data-event-emoji-next="📅"
  href="{{ link | default: routes.all_products_collection_url }}"
  aria-label="{{ line1 | strip_html }} {{ line2 | strip_html }}"
>
  <span class="hero-event-badge-emoji" aria-hidden="true">{{ emoji }}</span>
  <span class="hero-event-badge-title">{{ line1 }}</span>
  <span class="hero-event-badge-sub">{{ line2 }}</span>
</a>
{% style %}
  .hero-event-badge[hidden] { display: none; }
  .hero-event-badge[data-event-state] { gap: 4px; }
  .hero-event-badge[data-event-state] .hero-event-badge-emoji { font-size: 24px; }
  .hero-event-badge[data-event-state] .hero-event-badge-title {
    font-size: 13px;
    line-height: 1.12;
    letter-spacing: 0.01em;
    overflow-wrap: anywhere;
  }
  .hero-event-badge[data-event-state] .hero-event-badge-sub {
    max-width: 118px;
    font-size: 10.5px;
    line-height: 1.25;
  }
{% endstyle %}
